@page "/hypergeometric"

<PageTitle>Hypergeometric Calculator - Card Game Calculator</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">Hypergeometric Calculator</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-6" Color="Color.Secondary">
    Calculate the probability of drawing specific cards from your deck.
</MudText>

<MudExpansionPanels Class="mb-6" MultiExpansion="true">
    <MudExpansionPanel Text="Theory & Math">
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            The <strong>hypergeometric distribution</strong> models the number of target cards \(X\) drawn
            when \(n\) cards are drawn <em>without replacement</em> from a deck of \(N\) cards containing
            \(K\) instances of the target.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-1">Probability of exactly k instances</MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ P(X = k) = \frac{\binom{K}{k}\,\binom{N-K}{n-k}}{\binom{N}{n}} $$
        </div>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            where \(\binom{a}{b} = \frac{a!}{b!\,(a-b)!}\) is the binomial coefficient — the number of
            ways to choose \(b\) items from \(a\) items without regard to order.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-1">Cumulative forms</MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ P(X \geq k) = \sum_{i=k}^{\min(K,\,n)} P(X = i) \qquad \text{(at least } k \text{ instances)} $$
        </div>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ P(X \leq k) = \sum_{i=0}^{k} P(X = i) \qquad \text{(at most } k \text{ instances)} $$
        </div>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mt-4 mb-2">Parameters</MudText>
        <MudText>\(N\) — total cards in the deck</MudText>
        <MudText>\(K\) — instances of the target in the deck</MudText>
        <MudText>\(n\) — cards drawn (e.g. opening hand size)</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">\(k\) — exact number of instances drawn</MudText>

        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" Dense="true" Class="mb-6">
            Because cards are drawn <strong>without replacement</strong>, each draw changes the composition of the
            remaining deck — successive draws are not independent. The hypergeometric distribution models this
            dependency exactly, unlike the binomial approximation which incorrectly assumes independence.
        </MudAlert>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">Assumptions &amp; Simplifications</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            The following simplifications are in effect. Verify that they are acceptable for your use case
            before relying on the results.
        </MudText>
        <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem;" class="mb-6">
            <li><strong>Perfect shuffle</strong> — the deck is treated as uniformly randomly ordered. Imperfect shuffling that causes clumping or bias is not modeled.</li>
            <li class="mt-2"><strong>No mulligans</strong> — the draw is modeled as a single snapshot of <em>n</em> cards from the deck. Mulligans, which change the effective hand composition, are not accounted for. Use the Mulligan &amp; Looting Calculator for mulligan-aware estimates.</li>
            <li class="mt-2"><strong>Cards within the target group are interchangeable</strong> — only the instance count matters; individual card names within the group are not distinguished.</li>
            <li class="mt-2"><strong>No sequencing effects</strong> — scry, fetch lands, cantrips, and other library-manipulation effects are not modeled. The <em>n</em> drawn cards are assumed to come from a freshly shuffled, unfiltered library.</li>
        </ul>

        <MudDivider Class="mb-4" />
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">Optimal Instances Advisor</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            The Advisor inverts the hypergeometric question. Instead of computing \(P(X \geq k)\) for a
            fixed deck count \(K\), it finds the <em>minimum</em> \(K^*\) needed to meet a target
            probability \(p^*\):
        </MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ K^* = \min\!\left\{\, K \in \{1,\ldots,N\} \;:\; P(X \geq k) \geq p^* \,\right\} $$
        </div>
        <MudText>
            <em>Instances</em> refers to all cards that fulfil the same role — they need not be identical cards.
            In a singleton format, a "removal package" of ten different spells still contributes ten instances
            to this calculation.
        </MudText>
    </MudExpansionPanel>

    <MudExpansionPanel Text="How to Use">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">Hypergeometric Calculator</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            Set the four parameters describing your deck scenario and press <strong>Calculate</strong>.
            The bar chart shows the full probability distribution; the highlighted bar corresponds to
            your chosen desired instances.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Example — Lightning Bolt in Standard</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-2">
            Your deck has 4 instances of Lightning Bolt in 60 cards. What is the probability of drawing
            at least one instance in your opening hand of 7?
        </MudText>
        <ol style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <li>Deck Size: <strong>60</strong></li>
            <li>Instances in Deck: <strong>4</strong></li>
            <li>Cards Drawn: <strong>7</strong></li>
            <li>Desired Instances: <strong>1</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            The <em>At Least 1</em> result gives your answer — approximately <strong>39.95%</strong>.
        </MudText>

        <MudDivider Class="mb-4" />
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">Optimal Instances Advisor</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            Enter a target probability and the minimum number of instances you want in hand, then press
            <strong>Find Optimal Instances</strong>. The table shows the probability for each instance
            count, with the recommended minimum highlighted in green.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Example — Card Draw in Commander</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-2">
            You are building a Commander deck (99 cards). You want at least one piece of card draw in
            your opening hand of 7 at least <strong>80%</strong> of the time. How many card-draw spells
            do you need?
        </MudText>
        <ol style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <li>Select the <strong>100-card Singleton</strong> format — Deck Size becomes 99, Cards Drawn becomes 7.</li>
            <li>Target Probability: <strong>80%</strong></li>
            <li>Desired in Hand: <strong>1</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <MudText>
            Press <strong>Find Optimal Instances</strong>. The Recommended row shows the minimum count needed —
            roughly <strong>10 instances</strong> for an 80% target in a 7-card hand from a 99-card deck.
        </MudText>
    </MudExpansionPanel>
</MudExpansionPanels>

<MudGrid>
    <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
        <MudCard Elevation="2">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Parameters</MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_deckSize" Label="Deck Size" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="1" Max="999" HelperText="Total cards in your deck" Class="mb-4" />
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_instancesInDeck" Label="Instances in Deck" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="0" Max="@_deckSize" HelperText="Instances of the target in your deck" Class="mb-4" />
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_cardsDrawn" Label="Cards Drawn" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="1" Max="@_deckSize" HelperText="Cards drawn (e.g. opening hand size)" Class="mb-4" />
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_desiredInstances" Label="Desired Instances" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="0" Max="@Math.Min(_instancesInDeck, _cardsDrawn)"
                    HelperText="How many instances you want to see" />
            </MudCardContent>
            <MudCardActions Class="flex-column px-4 pb-4 pt-0">
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" OnClick="Calculate" FullWidth="true"
                    StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Calculate" Class="mb-2">
                    Calculate
                </MudButton>
                <MudTooltip Text="Resets Deck Size, Cards Drawn, and Instances in Deck to the defaults of the currently selected format. Clears the current results.">
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="ResetToFormat" FullWidth="true"
                        StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.RestartAlt">
                        Reset to chosen format
                    </MudButton>
                </MudTooltip>
            </MudCardActions>
        </MudCard>

        @if (_calculated)
        {
            <MudCard Elevation="2" Class="mt-4">
                <MudCardHeader>
                    <CardHeaderContent>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Results</MudText>
                    </CardHeaderContent>
                </MudCardHeader>
                <MudCardContent Class="pa-0">
                    <MudList T="string" Dense="true">
                        <MudListItem>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">Exactly @_desiredInstances @InstancesLabel(_desiredInstances)</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Color="Color.Primary">@_exactProb.ToString("P2")</MudText>
                        </MudListItem>
                        <MudDivider />
                        <MudListItem>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">At least @_desiredInstances @InstancesLabel(_desiredInstances)</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Color="Color.Primary">@_atLeastProb.ToString("P2")</MudText>
                        </MudListItem>
                        <MudDivider />
                        <MudListItem>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary">At most @_desiredInstances @InstancesLabel(_desiredInstances)</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Color="Color.Primary">@_atMostProb.ToString("P2")</MudText>
                        </MudListItem>
                    </MudList>
                </MudCardContent>
            </MudCard>
        }
        <MudCard Elevation="2" Class="mt-4">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Optimal Instances Advisor</MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_targetProbability" Label="Target probability (%)"
                    Variant="Variant.Outlined" Min="1" Max="99" Class="mb-4"
                    HelperText="Minimum chance of drawing the desired instances" />
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_advisorDesiredInHand" Label="Desired in hand"
                    Variant="Variant.Outlined" Min="1" Max="@_cardsDrawn"
                    HelperText="Instances you want to see in your opening hand" />
            </MudCardContent>
            <MudCardActions Class="flex-column px-4 pb-4 pt-0">
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Secondary" OnClick="RunAdvisor"
                    FullWidth="true" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Search">
                    Find Optimal Instances
                </MudButton>
            </MudCardActions>
        </MudCard>

        @if (_advisorCalculated)
        {
            <MudCard Elevation="2" Class="mt-4">
                <MudCardHeader>
                    <CardHeaderContent>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Advisor Results</MudText>
                        @if (_advisorMinInstances.HasValue)
                        {
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                                Minimum @_advisorMinInstances instance@(_advisorMinInstances == 1 ? "" : "s") for &ge;@_targetProbability% drawing @_cardsDrawn cards
                            </MudText>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Error">
                                Target not achievable within the deck.
                            </MudText>
                        }
                    </CardHeaderContent>
                </MudCardHeader>
                <MudCardContent Class="pa-0">
                    <MudTable Items="_advisorRows" Dense="true" Hover="true">
                        <HeaderContent>
                            <MudTh>Instances in deck</MudTh>
                            <MudTh>Probability</MudTh>
                            <MudTh></MudTh>
                        </HeaderContent>
                        <RowTemplate>
                            <MudTd>@context.Instances</MudTd>
                            <MudTd>
                                <MudText Color="@(context.MeetsTarget ? Color.Success : Color.Inherit)">
                                    @context.Probability.ToString("P2")
                                </MudText>
                            </MudTd>
                            <MudTd>
                                @if (context.Instances == _advisorMinInstances)
                                {
                                    <MudChip T="string" Color="Color.Success" Size="Size.Small">Recommended</MudChip>
                                }
                                else if (context.MeetsTarget)
                                {
                                    <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Check" Color="Color.Success" Size="Size.Small" />
                                }
                            </MudTd>
                        </RowTemplate>
                    </MudTable>
                </MudCardContent>
            </MudCard>
        }
    </MudItem>

    <MudItem xs="12" md="8">
        <MudCard Elevation="2">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Probability Distribution</MudText>
                    @if (_calculated)
                    {
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                            Drawing from @_deckSize cards (@_instancesInDeck instances), @_cardsDrawn drawn
                        </MudText>
                    }
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                @if (_calculated)
                {
                    <PlotlyChart Config="_chartConfig" Layout="_chartLayout" Data="_chartData" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudPaper Class="d-flex align-center justify-center" Style="height:300px;" Elevation="0">
                        <MudText Color="Color.Secondary">Press Calculate to see the distribution.</MudText>
                    </MudPaper>
                }
            </MudCardContent>
        </MudCard>
    </MudItem>
</MudGrid>
